This is a classic dynamic programming problem. We need to count the number of distinct subsequences of S, which is the same as the number of distinct subsequences of S[:-1] plus the number of distinct subsequences of S[:-1] that end with S[-1]. We can use a recursive approach to solve this problem, but we’ll need to memoize the results to avoid recalculating them.
